I went to one of those "Tobacco Use Only / Assorted Antiques" stores
today, a really nice one that has pretty much anything you need, if
you're willing to pay high prices (think One-Eyed Sam's but with a
smaller markup).  At the end of a shelf of patches, incense, fimo,
stuffed animals, and dog collars with half naked women on the packages,
I notice...well, the best way i can describe it is like this...

Things that are here:
a lamp
a lamp
a lamp
a lamp
a lamp
a lamp
--More--

Now I see why lamps shouldn't stack... they're so different!  They were
all brass, 6-10 inches tall, long, slender, beautiful lamps, shaped and
decorated uniquely.  Could I get a wish today?!!!

On a side note, I had not brought any scrolls of remove curse with me.
I think I have one in a large box named My Apartment, but it's the
weekend so I'm adhering to the illiterate conduct.  I consider reading
and posting to RGRN equivalent to reading the Book of the Dead... it
doesn't break the conduct!

